y discovery, verification, or restart polling. Restart evidence is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart data and boot ID, acknowledgement, bounded unavailability, a different post-restart boot ID, and recovered data/platform state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d2bcbe9d665f4ae2","cmd-83cf9217e48d40e3","cmd-59d09f155ff448db","cmd-780b6be5c74741a4","cmd-2a3d57d9e4994ceb","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre/post and archive-to-live verification. The requested invoices were selectively restored with correct bytes and modes, the newer customer register remained unchanged, unrelated archive entries were excluded, and the legacy OS/kernel were retained. The mandatory restart protocol also demonstrates persistence and recovery.","limitations":["Systemd failed-unit observation was unsupported on this legacy platform; no task service or cluster was involved, and SSH recovery plus post-restart data and platform checks provide the applicable recovery evidence."]}
